          "value": "12791985"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "title": [
    {
      "type": "Text",
      "value": {
        "string": "Prolonged cell cycle arrest in response to DNA damage in yeast requires the maintenance of DNA damage signaling and the spindle assembly checkpoint"
      }
    }
  ],
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "Section",
      "id": "s1",
      "sectionType": "Introduction",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "Heading",
          "level": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "Introduction"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "Paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "DNA double-strand breaks (DSBs) are one of the most deleterious forms of DNA damage ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib35",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Mehta and Haber, 2014"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "). In response to DSBs, cells evoke the DNA damage checkpoint (DDC) to halt the metaphase to anaphase transition (known as the G"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Subscript",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "2"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "/M checkpoint). Activation of DDC gives cells an extended opportunity to repair DSBs and, therefore, prevents the inheritance of broken chromosomes, which can lead to aneuploidy, chromosome aberrations, and genome instability ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib62",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Waterman et al., 2020"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": ")."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "Paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "In budding yeast, a single irreparable DSB is sufficient to trigger the DDC through the activation of Mec1, a PI3K-like kinase and homolog of the mammalian ATR ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib30",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Mantiero et al., 2007"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib47",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Pellicioli et al., 2001"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "). Mec1 activation depends on 5’ to 3’ resection of the DSB ends that exposes single-stranded DNA (ssDNA), which is rapidly coated by the ssDNA binding protein, RPA (reviewed by "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib32",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Maréchal and Zou, 2015"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "). As resection proceeds, the PCNA-related 9-1-1 clamp, made up of Ddc1, Rad17, and Mec3, is loaded at the resected ss/dsDNA junction by the Rad24-Rfc2-5 clamp loader ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib15",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Ellison and Stillman, 2003"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib29",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Majka et al., 2006"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "). Mec1 is recruited to DSB sites via its obligate binding partner, Ddc2"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Superscript",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "ATRIP"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": " interacting with RPA-bound ssDNA ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib12",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Dubrana et al., 2007"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib68",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Zou and Elledge, 2003"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "). Following its localization to DSBs, Mec1’s kinase activity is stimulated by Dbp11, Dna2, and the Ddc1 subunit of the 9-1-1 clamp ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib42",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Navadgi-Patil and Burgers, 2009"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib36",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Melo et al., 2001"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "). Impairing Mec1’s kinase activity by the PI3K-like kinase inhibitor caffeine, by using temperature-sensitive Mec1 mutants or by degradation of Mec1’s binding partner Ddc2, rapidly extinguishes checkpoint signaling ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib47",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Pellicioli et al., 2001"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib57",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Tsabar et al., 2015"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib60",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Vaze et al., 2002"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "), illustrating that continual Mec1 activity is needed to activate and sustain DDC. In contrast to Mec1, yeast’s other PI3K-like kinase, Tel1, the homolog of mammalian ATM, is dispensable for DDC activation and maintenance, as "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Emphasis",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "TEL1"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": " deletion only shortens damage-induced cell cycle arrest by a few hours ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib12",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Dubrana et al., 2007"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": ")."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "Paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "Following the induction of a DSB, numerous proteins are phosphorylated either directly by Mec1 or by the downstream effector kinases Rad53 and Chk1 (human CHK2 and CHK1), which are themselves Mec1 substrates ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib23",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Lanz et al., 2019"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib55",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Smolka et al., 2007"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "). Mec1 and Tel1 substrates also include histone H2A-S129, called γ-H2AX, which spreads on both sides of the DSB via two distinct mechanisms ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib49",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Rogakou et al., 1998"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib54",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Shroff et al., 2004"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "). γ-H2AX then recruits the scaffold protein Rad9, which brings the effector kinase Rad53 in close proximity to Mec1 for activation ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib13",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Durocher et al., 1999"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib16",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Emili, 1998"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib52",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Schwartz et al., 2002"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "). Activated Rad53 then amplifies the DDC signal through autophosphorylation in trans, also stimulating the transcription regulator Dun1 kinase, while restraining the degradation of Pds1 (securin) to inhibit mitosis ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib6",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Chen et al., 2007"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib17",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Fiorani et al., 2008"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib46",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Pellicioli et al., 1999"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib58",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Usui and Petrini, 2007"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib63",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Yam et al., 2020"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": ")."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "Paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "In addition to the DDC, unattached kinetochores can induce cell cycle arrest through the activation of spindle assembly checkpoint (SAC) (reviewed by "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib41",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Musacchio, 2015"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "). Several studies have suggested a crosstalk between the SAC and the DDC. For example, deletion of SAC components "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Emphasis",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "MAD1"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": " or "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Emphasis",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "MAD2"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": " shortens the cell cycle arrest in response to DNA-damaging agents in the absence of DDC genes "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Emphasis",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "RAD9"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": " and "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Emphasis",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "RAD24"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": " ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib18",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Garber and Rine, 2002"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib22",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Kim and Burke, 2008"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "). Furthermore, "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Emphasis",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "MAD1, MAD2,"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": " or "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Emphasis",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "BUB1"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": " mutants arrest for less time than wild-type cells following the induction of a single persistent DSB ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib11",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Dotiwala et al., 2010"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "). In mouse oocytes, inhibition of the SAC overrides the activation of DDC-mediated metaphase arrest during the first meiotic division ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib31",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Marangos et al., 2015"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "). The mitotic exit network (MEN) is another signaling cascade activated during anaphase to promote cell cycle re-entry "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib33",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Matellán and Monje-Casas, 2020"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; therefore, defects in MEN lead to mitotic arrest in late anaphase ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib19",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Geymonat et al., 2002"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib4",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Bardin et al., 2000"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib53",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Shirayama et al., 1994"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "). In addition to SAC, MEN also communicates with the DDC in response to DNA damage. For instance, a key regulator of MEN, the heterodimer Bub2/Bfa1 complex, is modified in a Rad53 and Dun1-dependent manner following damage ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib20",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Hu et al., 2001"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "). Supporting the idea of crosstalk between MEN and DDC, our lab had shown that deletion of "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Emphasis",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "BUB2"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": " shortened the duration of the arrest in response to a single unrepaired DSB ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib11",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Dotiwala et al., 2010"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": ")."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "Paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "Here, we present new mechanistic insights into the "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Emphasis",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "maintenance"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": " of the cell cycle arrest following DNA damage by employing the auxin-inducible degron (AID) strategy to conditionally deplete DDC and SAC proteins. An advantage of the AID system, compared to null or temperature-sensitive mutants, is that AID-tagged proteins retain wild-type function until the addition of the plant hormone auxin (indole-3-acetic acid [IAA]), which triggers rapid degradation of AID-tagged proteins in the presence of the TIR1 E3 ubiquitin ligase ("
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib40",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Morawska and Ulrich, 2013"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "; "
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "Citation",
              "target": "bib43",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Nishimura et al., 2009"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "). To investigate how conditional depletion of DDC or SAC proteins alters the maintenance of cell cycle arrest, we engineered a yeast strain that permanently arrests due to the presence of two persistent DNA breaks. We find that the maintenance of the cell cycle arrest requires constant presence of some, but not all, checkpoint activation proteins. Surprisingly, we find that the DDC proteins that are essential to induce the cell cycle arrest and sustain it at the early stages of the arrest become dispensable nearly 15 hr after DNA damage induction. Conversely, SAC proteins are dispensable for the establishment and the initial steps of the cell cycle arrest but become essential at later stages of the DNA damage-dependent cell cycle arrest. Based on these findings, we posit that prolonged cell cycle arrest in response to DNA damage is sustained by both SAC and DDC; however, each checkpoint sustains the arrest at different stages."
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "Section",
      "id": "s2",
      "sectionType": "Results",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "Heading",
          "level": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "Results"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "Section",
          "id": "s2-1",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "Heading",
              "level": 2,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Measuring DNA damage checkpoint arrest and maintenance"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "To study the role of DDC initiation proteins in the "
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Emphasis",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "maintenance"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": " of the cell cycle arrest, we utilized the well-characterized strain JKM179 ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Citation",
                  "target": "bib25",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Lee et al., 1998"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "), in which the site-specific HO endonuclease is expressed from a "
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Emphasis",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "GAL1-10"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": " promoter ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Emphasis",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "GAL-HO"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": ") to induce a single DSB within the "
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Emphasis",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "MAT"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": " locus on chromosome III (referred to as the 1-DSB strain). In this 1-DSB strain, we inserted an additional HO cleavage site 52 kb from the centromere on chromosome IV to induce another DSB (referred to as the 2-DSB strain) ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Citation",
                  "target": "bib21",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Kim et al., 2007"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "; "
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Citation",
                  "target": "bib25",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Lee et al., 1998"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "). At both loci, HO-mediated cleavage after galactose induction is nearly complete within 30–45 min ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Citation",
                  "target": "bib26",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Lee et al., 2014"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "). In both strains, we also deleted the "
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Emphasis",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "HML"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": " and "
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Emphasis",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "HMR"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": " donors to prevent repair by homologous recombination. With continuous "
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Emphasis",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "HO"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": " expression, nonhomologous end-joining occurs in only 0.2% of these cells ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Citation",
                  "target": "bib39",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Moore and Haber, 1996"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "), thus both DSBs are essentially irreparable."
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Following the induction of 2 DSBs, we monitored cell cycle arrest in four ways: (1) with an adaptation time-course assay where we micromanipulated individual G"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Subscript",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "1"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": " cells on agar plates and scored the percentage of cells that are able to re-enter mitosis ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Citation",
                  "target": "bib25",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Lee et al., 1998"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "), (2) by monitoring the percentage of G"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Subscript",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "2"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "/M-arrested cells in liquid culture based on cell morphology ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figure 1A"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig1",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "), (3) by monitoring nuclear division by DAPI staining of nuclei, and (4) by assaying Rad53 phosphorylation by western blot ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Citation",
                  "target": "bib47",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Pellicioli et al., 2001"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": ")."
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Figure",
              "id": "fig1",
              "label": "1",
              "labelAutomatically": false,
              "caption": [
                {
                  "type": "Paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "Measuring checkpoint arrest in 1-DSB and 2-DSB strains. "
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "A"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") Morphological categories of budding yeast cells using brightfield microscopy and DAPI staining were used to determine G"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Subscript",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "2"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "/M arrest. Cells that arrest at G2/M shift toward a large bud state. G"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Subscript",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "2"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "/M-arrested cells that progress into anaphase. ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "B"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") Adaptation assay with 1-DSB strain on a YEP-Gal plate. G"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Subscript",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "2"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "/M arrest was determined based on cell morphology as shown in ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "A"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "). Data are shown from three independent experiments, error bars represent standard error of the mean (SEM). ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "C"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") Profile of DAPI-stained cells in a 1-DSB strain after DNA damage induction in liquid culture. Cells were grouped based on cell morphology and DAPI staining profiles, as explained below the graphs. ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "D"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") Rad53 phosphorylation kinetics in 1-DSB strain by western blotting. Samples collected after the induction of DNA damage during the time-course experiment and blotted with α-Rad53 to monitor DDC signaling. α-Rad53 can both detect unphosphorylated and hyperphosphorylated Rad53 species. TIR1-Myc was detected with α-Myc and serves as a loading control. ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "E"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") Same as ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "B"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") for a 2-DSB strain. ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "F"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") Same as ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "C"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") with a 2-DSB strain. ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "G"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") Same as ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "D"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") with a 2-DSB strain."
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Supplement",
                  "id": "fig1sdata1",
                  "label": "Figure 1—source data 1.",
                  "labelAutomatically": false,
                  "workType": "Dataset",
                  "caption": [
                    {
                      "type": "Heading",
