        },
        {
          "type": "Section",
          "id": "s2-5",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "Heading",
              "level": 2,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Ddc2 and Rad53’s role in maintaining arrest become dispensable in extended G"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Subscript",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "2"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "/M arrest"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Previously, we reported that Ddc2 protein abundance initially increases over time as after the induction of a single DNA break, which is followed by near-complete depletion of Ddc2 around the time that cells adapt ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Citation",
                  "target": "bib37",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Memisoglu et al., 2019"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "). Given that Ddc2 overexpression leads to permanent cell cycle arrest following DNA damage ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Citation",
                  "target": "bib7",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Clerici et al., 2001"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "), we concluded that Ddc2 abundance is intimately tied to the duration of the arrest. Here, we asked whether the presence of 2 DSBs instead of a single DSB would lead to an increase in Ddc2 protein abundance and, therefore, the permanent cell cycle arrest. We examined the levels of Ddc2 in both 1- and 2-DSB strains following DNA damage but did not detect a difference in the changes of abundance of Ddc2 protein ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figure 5—figure supplement 1"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig5s1",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "), even though cells adapt to 1 DSBs and remained terminally arrested after 2 DSBs ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figure 1A–D"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig1",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": ")."
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "If Ddc2 activity is essential to maintain the cell cycle arrest in the 2-DSB strain, then degradation of Ddc2-AID around the time wild-type cells adapt to a single DNA break should interrupt the permanent cell cycle arrest and trigger cell cycle re-entry. We find that complete depletion of Ddc2-AID 15 hr after the induction of 2 DSBs leads to diminished Rad53 hyperphosphorylation ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figure 5A"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig5",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "). However, surprisingly, Ddc2-AID degradation did not alter the percentage of G"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Subscript",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "2"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "/M-arrested cells even 9 hr after Ddc2 depletion ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figure 5A"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig5",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "). Furthermore, despite the diminished Rad53 phosphorylation, Ddc2-AID cells mostly remained arrested in G"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Subscript",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "2"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "/M after the depletion of Ddc2-AID at 15 hr as illustrated by DAPI staining ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figure 5B"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig5",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "), in contrast to Ddc2-AID depletion soon after induction of 2 DSBs, which causes cells to rapidly resume mitosis ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figure 2A"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig2",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "). These results hint that the maintenance of the permanent cell cycle arrest in response to 2 DSBs at later stages could be independent of the DDC signaling."
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Figure",
              "id": "fig5",
              "label": "5",
              "labelAutomatically": false,
              "caption": [
                {
                  "type": "Paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "Ddc2 and Rad53 are dispensable for >24 hr checkpoint arrest. "
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "A"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") Percentage of G"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Subscript",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "2"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "/M-arrested cells for 2-DSB "
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Emphasis",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "DDC2-AID"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": " after HO induction. Data is shown from three trials with standard error of the mean (SEM). Western blot probed with α-Rad53 and α-Myc. α-Rad53 shows both an unphosphorylated protein and multiple phosphorylated species. α-Myc shows Ddc2-AID degradation and TIR1-Myc as a loading control. ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "B"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") Profile of DAPI-stained cells in a 2-DSB "
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Emphasis",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "DDC2-AID"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": " strain after HO induction. Cells were categorized based on cell morphology and number of DAPI signals. ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "C"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") Percentage of G"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Subscript",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "2"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "/M-arrested cells for 2-DSB "
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Emphasis",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "RAD53-AID TIR1(F74G"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") after HO induction. 5-Ph-IAA was added 4 hr after HO induction. Data is shown from three trials with standard error of the mean (SEM). Western blot probed with α-Rad53, α-Myc, and α-Pgk1. α-Rad53 shows both an unphosphorylated protein and multiple phosphorylated species. α-Myc shows Rad53-AID degradation. α-Pgk1 probed as a loading control. ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "D"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") Same as ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "C"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") where 5-Ph-IAA was added 15 hr after HO induction. ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "E"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") Percentage G"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Subscript",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "2"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "/M-arrested cells for 2-DSB "
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Emphasis",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "RAD9-AID"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": " plus pRad9-AID after HO induction. Data shown from three trials with standard error of the mean (SEM). Western blot probed with α-Rad53 and α-Myc. α-Rad53 shows both an unphosphorylated protein and multiple phosphorylated species. α-Myc shows Rad9-AID degradation and TIR1-Myc as a loading control. α-Pgk1 probed as a loading control."
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
