                }
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "ImageObject",
                  "contentUrl": "elife-94334-fig5-figsupp1-v1.tif",
                  "mediaType": "image/tiff"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "We then asked whether other DDC factors such as Rad9, Rad24, and Rad53 are dispensable for the prolonged arrest following the induction of 2 DSBs. However, as noted above, AID-tagged DDC activation proteins were unable to maintain this prolonged arrest in a 2-DSB strain even in the absence of IAA, which precludes their use in this analysis. To be able to study the contribution of these DDC factors in prolonged cell cycle arrest, we turned to the AID version 2 (AID2) system ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Citation",
                  "target": "bib64",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Yesbolatova et al., 2020"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "). To this end, we integrated a TIR1-F74G point mutation and used 5-phenyl-IAA (5-Ph-IAA) instead of IAA to lower the basal degradation of AID-tagged proteins. Switching to the AID2 system did not fully restore function to "
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Emphasis",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "RAD9-AID2"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": " and "
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Emphasis",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "RAD24-AID2"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": " strains as they mostly adapted after 24 hr after the exposure to DNA damage, but 87% of "
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Emphasis",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "RAD53-AID2"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": " cells remained in G"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Subscript",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "2"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "/M arrest at 24 hr ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figure 2—figure supplement 1C"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig2s1",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "). Using Rad53-AID2, we then asked whether Rad53 is required for extended G"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Subscript",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "2"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "/M arrest in response to 2 DSBs. Rapid depletion of Rad53-AID2 with 5-Ph-IAA 4 hr after DSB induction led cells to escape G"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Subscript",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "2"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "/M arrest, but as with the "
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Emphasis",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "RAD53-AID"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": " strain, we detected a 4 hr delay in cell cycle re-entry, confirming our previous results ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figures 2D"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig2",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": " and "
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "5C"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig5",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "). However, degradation of Rad53-AID2 15 hr after DSB induction did not prompt cell cycle re-entry even 9 hr after complete depletion of Rad53 ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figure 5D"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig5",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": ", "
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Table 1"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#table1",
                  "jatsRefType": "table"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "), akin to what we observe following the depletion of Ddc2-AID ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figure 5A and B"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig5",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": ")."
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
