                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "To show that the late stages of the permanent cell cycle arrest in response to 2 DSBs is independent of DDC and dependent on SAC, we inactivated DDC by depleting Ddc2-AID together with Mad2-AID. Although the simultaneous depletion of Ddc2-AID and Mad2-AID led to Rad53 dephosphorylation as detected by western blotting, we found no statistically significant difference in the percentage of cells escaping G"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Subscript",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "2"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "/M arrest in response to "
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Emphasis",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "DDC2-AID MAD2-AID"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": " double depletion strain compared to Mad2-AID alone ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figure 6—figure supplement 3"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig6s3",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": " and "
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Table 1"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#table1",
                  "jatsRefType": "table"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "). Collectively, our findings indicate that DDC initiates and sustains the cell cycle arrest approximately for 15 hr following DNA damage, but after that DDC becomes dispensable and the permanent arrest is sustained by SAC."
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "Section",
          "id": "s2-7",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "Heading",
              "level": 2,
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "Mitotic exit network proteins Bfa1 and Bub2 have different roles in the DDR"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "To investigate the possible contribution of the MEN to the maintenance of the extended cell cycle arrest in response to 2 DSBs, we appended AID tags to upstream MEN proteins Bub2 and Bfa1. Degradation of Bub2-AID both 4 hr and 15 hr after induction of 2 DSBs suppressed G"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Subscript",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "2"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "/M arrest ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figure 7A"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig7",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": ", "
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figure 7—figure supplement 1A and B"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig7s1",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "), akin to what we observe following Mad1-AID or Mad2-AID depletion ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figure 6A and B"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig6",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "). In contrast to Bub2-AID, we see that Bfa1-AID degradation did not trigger a significant release from G"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Subscript",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "2"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "/M arrest and did not alter the phosphorylation of Rad53 ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figure 7B"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig7",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": ", "
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figure 7—figure supplement 1C–E"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig7s1",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "). Analysis of cell cycle distribution with DAPI staining showed that neither the inactivation of Bub2 nor Bfa1 led to the accumulation of a significant number of cells with two separate DAPI-staining nuclei, which is indicative of mitotic exit defects ("
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figure 7B and D"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig7",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": ", "
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "Link",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "Figure 7—figure supplement 1B, D, and F"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "target": "#fig7s1",
                  "jatsRefType": "fig"
                },
                {
                  "type": "Text",
                  "value": {
                    "string": "). These results imply that although Bub2 and Bfa1 have interdependent functions for MEN signaling, they carry out independent roles in response to DNA damage."
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "Figure",
              "id": "fig7",
              "label": "7",
              "labelAutomatically": false,
              "caption": [
                {
                  "type": "Paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "Degradation of Bub2 but not Bfa1 at 15 hr releases cells from checkpoint arrest. "
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "A"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") Percentage of G"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Subscript",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "2"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": "/M-arrested cells for 2-DSB "
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Emphasis",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "BUB2-AID"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": " after HO induction. Data is shown from three trials with standard error of the mean (SEM). Western blot probed with α-Rad53 and α-Myc. α-Rad53 shows both an unphosphorylated protein and multiple phosphorylated species. α-Myc shows Bub2-AID degradation and TIR1-Myc as a loading control. ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "B"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") Profile of DAPI-stained cells in a 2-DSB "
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Emphasis",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "BUB2-AID"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": " strain after HO induction. Liquid cultures were split 15 hr after HO induction and treated with either IAA or ethanol. Cells were scored based on cell morphology and number of DAPI signals. ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "C"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") Same as ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "A"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") for 2-DSB "
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Emphasis",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "BFA1-AID"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ". ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "D"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": {
                        "string": ") Same as ("
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Strong",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "Text",
                          "value": {
                            "string": "B"
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Text",
